			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1627535">
									

<p>For something to be exponential, the variable needs to <strong>be</strong> the exponent. It's not enough to just have an exponent. Example: x<sup>2</sup> is not exponential, but 2<sup>x</sup> is exponential.</p>
<p>y=v+x<sup>5.04</sup> is not exponential growth.<br />
y=v+5.04<sup>x</sup>, however, would be exponential growth.</p>
<p>Of course, if you make this change, the object will increase <strong>much</strong> faster than you've described, so you might want to reduce the value, 5.04.</p>

